Body:
The link was broken, the correct one is: https://open-code.ai/en/docs/modes which says it is deprecated now. "Caution: Modes are now configured through the agent option in the opencode config. The mode option is now deprecated. [Learn more](https://open-code.ai/en/docs/agents).". As I understand we can now change our defined agent's system prompt:
```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "agent": {
    "build": {
      "mode": "primary",
      "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-20250514",
      "prompt": "{file:./prompts/build.txt}",
      "tools": {
        "write": true,
        "edit": true,
        "bash": true
      }
    },
    "plan": {
      "mode": "primary",
      "model": "anthropic/claude-haiku-4-20250514",
      "tools": {
        "write": false,
        "edit": false,
        "bash": false
      }
    },
    "code-reviewer": {
      "description": "Reviews code for best practices and potential issues",
      "mode": "subagent",
      "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-20250514",
      "prompt": "**You are a code reviewer. Focus on security, performance, and maintainability.**",
      "tools": {
        "write": false,
        "edit": false
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Even though this example does not showcase, we should change the plan and the build agent's system prompts.
